{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato","suddhaso"],"title":"17. Anger","html":"<section class='range'  id='dhp221-234'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Khuddakanikāya </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Minor Collection </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Collection of Minor Texts </span></li>\n<li class='subdivision'><span class='root'>Dhammapada </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Sayings of the Dhamma 221–234 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Verses of Dhamma </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='range-title'><span class='root'>Kodhavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>17. Anger </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>The Anger Chapter </span></h1></header>\n<article id='dhp221'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Rohinīkhattiyakaññāvatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Kodhaṁ jahe vippajaheyya mānaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Give up anger, get rid of conceit, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Abandon anger, discard conceit, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Saṁyojanaṁ sabbamatikkameyya; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and escape every fetter. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>completely transcend the fetter; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Taṁ nāmarūpasmimasajjamānaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Sufferings don’t befall one who has nothing, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Not adhering to mind and body, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Akiñcanaṁ nānupatanti dukkhā. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>not clinging to name and form. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>possessing nothing, one does not fall into suffering. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp222'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Aññatarabhikkhuvatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yo ve uppatitaṁ kodhaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>When anger surges like a lurching chariot, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>When anger arises, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>rathaṁ bhantaṁva vāraye; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>keep it in check. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>one who stops it like a runaway cart - </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Tamahaṁ sārathiṁ brūmi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>That’s what I call a charioteer; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>That is the one I call a charioteer; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>rasmiggāho itaro jano. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>others just hold the reins. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>other people just hold the reins. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp223'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Uttarāupāsikavatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Akkodhena jine kodhaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Defeat anger with kindness, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>By means of non-anger one defeats anger, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>asādhuṁ sādhunā jine; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>villainy with virtue, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>by means of excellence one defeats non-excellence, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Jine kadariyaṁ dānena, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>stinginess with giving, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>by means of generosity one defeats stinginess, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>saccenālikavādinaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and lies with truth. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>by means of truth one defeats lies. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp224'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Mahāmoggallānapañhavatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Saccaṁ bhaṇe na kujjheyya, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Speak the truth, do not be angry, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Speak the truth, do not get angry, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>dajjā appampi yācito; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and give when asked, if only a little. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>and give - even just a little bit - when asked; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Etehi tīhi ṭhānehi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>By these three means, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>by means of these three things </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>gacche devāna santike. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>you may enter the presence of the gods. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>you will enter the presence of the angels. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp225'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Buddhapitubrāhmaṇavatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Ahiṁsakā ye munayo, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Those harmless sages, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Those sages who are harmless, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>niccaṁ kāyena saṁvutā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>always restrained in body, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>who are always physically restrained, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Te yanti accutaṁ ṭhānaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>go to the state that does not pass, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>go to the undying state </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>yattha gantvā na socare. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>where there is no sorrow. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>where they do not sorrow. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp226'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Puṇṇadāsīvatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Sadā jāgaramānānaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Always wakeful, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>When one is always wakeful, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>ahorattānusikkhinaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>practicing night and day, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>training day and night, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Nibbānaṁ adhimuttānaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>focused only on extinguishment, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>and intent upon Nibbāna, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>atthaṁ gacchanti āsavā. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>their defilements come to an end. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>their defilements disappear. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp227'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Atulaupāsakavatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Porāṇametaṁ atula, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>It’s always been this way, Atula, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>This is an incomparably ancient truth, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>netaṁ ajjatanāmiva; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>it’s not just today. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>not just the way it is today: </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Nindanti tuṇhimāsīnaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>They blame you when you’re silent, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>they criticize those who are silent, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>nindanti bahubhāṇinaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>they blame you when you speak a lot, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>they criticize those who speak a lot, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Mitabhāṇimpi nindanti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and even when you speak just right: </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>they criticize those who speak moderately; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>natthi loke anindito. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>no one in the world escapes blame. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>there is no one in the world who is not criticized. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp228'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Na cāhu na ca bhavissati, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>There never was, nor will be, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>It has not been, it will not be, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>na cetarahi vijjati; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>nor is there today, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>and it is not now the case </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Ekantaṁ nindito poso, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>someone who is wholly praised </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>that anyone is exclusively criticized </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>ekantaṁ vā pasaṁsito. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>or wholly blamed. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>or exclusively praised. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp229'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yañce viññū pasaṁsanti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>If, after watching them day in day out, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>The discerning praise one who, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>anuvicca suve suve; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>discerning people praise </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>when observed day after day, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Acchiddavuttiṁ medhāviṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>that sage of impeccable conduct, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>is known to have impeccable conduct, intelligence, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>paññāsīlasamāhitaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>endowed with ethics and wisdom; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>wisdom, morality, and concentration. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp230'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Nikkhaṁ jambonadasseva, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>like a pendant of Black Plum River gold, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Such a person is like a gold coin - </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>ko taṁ ninditumarahati; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>who is worthy to criticize them? </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>who would be worthy to criticize them? </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Devāpi naṁ pasaṁsanti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Even the gods praise them, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Even the angels praise such a person; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>brahmunāpi pasaṁsito. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and by the Divinity, too, they’re praised. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>even Brahmā praises such a person. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp231'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Chabbaggiyavatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Kāyappakopaṁ rakkheyya, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Guard against ill-tempered deeds, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Protect yourself from manifesting anger physically; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>kāyena saṁvuto siyā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>be restrained in body. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>practice physical self-restraint. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Kāyaduccaritaṁ hitvā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Giving up bad bodily conduct, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Having relinquished physical misconduct, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>kāyena sucaritaṁ care. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>conduct yourself well in body. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>practice good conduct with the body. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp232'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Vacīpakopaṁ rakkheyya, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Guard against ill-tempered words, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Protect yourself from manifesting anger verbally; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>vācāya saṁvuto siyā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>be restrained in speech. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>practice verbal self-restraint. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Vacīduccaritaṁ hitvā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Giving up bad verbal conduct, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Having relinquished verbal misconduct, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>vācāya sucaritaṁ care. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>conduct yourself well in speech. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>practice good conduct with speech. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp233'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Manopakopaṁ rakkheyya, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Guard against ill-tempered thoughts, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Protect yourself from manifesting anger mentally; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>manasā saṁvuto siyā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>be restrained in mind. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>practice mental self-restraint. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Manoduccaritaṁ hitvā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Giving up bad mental conduct, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Having relinquished mental misconduct, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>manasā sucaritaṁ care. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>conduct yourself well in mind. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>practice good conduct with the mind. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp234'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Kāyena saṁvutā dhīrā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>An attentive one is restrained in body </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>The steadfast are self-restrained physically, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>atho vācāya saṁvutā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>restrained also in speech, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>verbally, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Manasā saṁvutā dhīrā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>in thought, too, they are restrained: </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>and mentally; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>te ve suparisaṁvutā. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>they are restrained in every way. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>they are well-restrained in every way. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endvagga'><span class='root'>Kodhavaggo sattarasamo. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></p></article></section>"}
